   "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Imageability in Window Views</title>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"sp-scheme\">\n{\n \"format\": \"sp-scheme-package\",\n \"spScheme\": \"2.0\",\n \"survey\": {\n  \"title\": \"Imageability in Window Views\",\n  \"description\": \"Faithful replication with the original photographs: five window views of residential neighbourhoods in Ljubljana, Slovenia (N1 Novo Brdo, N2 Litostrojski bloki, N3 Mostec, N4 Štepanjsko naselje, N5 Zupančičeva jama), each photographed from where a resident looks out of the window at the opposite façade, with different amounts and kinds of greenery between the buildings. Participants are told the paper's meaning of imageability (characteristic and qualitative elements that, when seen in a specific location, attract attention, evoke pleasant feelings and create a memorable impression) and, for each view, choose from the paper's eight indicators: façade prominence and visibility, richness and articulation of the building, readability of the open space, multi-layered greenery, texture of surfaces, buildings with identifiers, vibrancy and dynamics of the ambiance, open views into the wider space. As in the paper's two survey approaches, each participant is randomly given either single choice (one indicator per view, SA1) or multiple choice (any number, SA2). Field of study is asked at the end. Rebuilt from Fikfak, Zbašnik-Senegačnik & Drobne (2022), Greenery as an Element of Imageability in Window Views, Land 11(12): 2157, with the photographs cropped from its Figure 2 and the indicators and procedure from its Section 2.3 (CC BY 4.0). Image ids: N1-N5; group records SA1 or SA2; answers are in imageability_single (SA1) or imageability_multi (SA2), keyed by view. Analysis as in the paper: share of responses for each indicator per view and survey approach, ranks of the indicators, the correlation of ranks between the two approaches, and a t-test of the rank differences of texture of surfaces against the other indicators; the paper (88 architecture and urbanism students) found similar rankings under both approaches (r = 0.786) except for texture of surfaces, multi-layered greenery among the most chosen indicators for the greener views (N2, N3, N5), façade prominence chosen most for N1 and, under single choice, open views into the wider space for N4. Differences from the original study: (1) the paper's first six questions on the need for a window and the importance of a good view are not included because their wording is not printed; (2) the paper gave the two approaches to two separate student groups (architecture students in a Moodle classroom, urbanism students on 1KA, both online in May 2022); here the approach is randomly assigned and anyone can take part; (3) the question wording, the instruction text and the view order (N1 to N5, as numbered in the paper) are ours; (4) the field-of-study question is ours; (5) the photographs are the figure copies (about 600 px wide), not the 2592 x 1944 px originals.\",\n  \"locale\": \"en\",\n  \"mediaFolders\": [\n   \"views\"\n  ],\n  \"pages\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"start\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"consent\",\n      \"name\": \"consent\",\n      \"title\": \"I agree to take part. Participation is voluntary and my answers are recorded anonymously for research.\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"labelTrue\": \"I agree\",\n      \"labelFalse\": \"I do not agree\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"group\",\n      \"title\": \"Survey approach (set by the page)\",\n      \"isRequired\": false,\n      \"visible\": false,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"SA1\",\n        \"text\": \"single choice\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"SA2\",\n        \"text\": \"multiple choice\"\n       }\n      ]\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"views\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"imageability_single\",\n      \"title\": \"Which element makes this window view imageable?\",\n      \"isRequired\": false,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I1\",\n        \"text\": \"Façade prominence and visibility\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I2\",\n        \"text\": \"Richness and articulation of the building\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I3\",\n        \"text\": \"Readability of the open space\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I4\",\n        \"text\": \"Multi-layered greenery\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I5\",\n        \"text\": \"Texture of surfaces\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I6\",\n        \"text\": \"Buildings with identifiers\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I7\",\n        \"text\": \"Vibrancy and dynamics of the ambiance\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I8\",\n        \"text\": \"Open views into the wider space\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"SA1 group: one indicator per view. Keyed by view (N1-N5).\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"checkbox\",\n      \"name\": \"imageability_multi\",\n      \"title\": \"Which elements make this window view imageable? Choose all that apply.\",\n      \"isRequired\": false,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I1\",\n        \"text\": \"Façade prominence and visibility\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I2\",\n        \"text\": \"Richness and articulation of the building\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I3\",\n        \"text\": \"Readability of the open space\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I4\",\n        \"text\": \"Multi-layered greenery\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I5\",\n        \"text\": \"Texture of surfaces\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I6\",\n        \"text\": \"Buildings with identifiers\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I7\",\n        \"text\": \"Vibrancy and dynamics of the ambiance\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"I8\",\n        \"text\": \"Open views into the wider space\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"SA2 group: any number of indicators per view. Keyed by view (N1-N5).\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"about\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"field\",\n      \"title\": \"What is your background?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"architecture\",\n        \"text\": \"Architecture (student or professional)\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"urbanism\",\n        \"text\": \"Urbanism / urban planning (student or professional)\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"other_design\",\n        \"text\": \"Another design or environment field\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"other\",\n        \"text\": \"Other\"\n       }\n      ]\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n }\n}\n</script>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"windowview-original\">{\"source\": \"Fikfak, Zbašnik-Senegačnik & Drobne (2022) Land 11: 2157\", \"n\": 88, \"indicators\": [[\"I1\", \"Façade prominence and visibility\"], [\"I2\", \"Richness and articulation of the building\"], [\"I3\", \"Readability of the open space\"], [\"I4\", \"Multi-layered greenery\"], [\"I5\", \"Texture of surfaces\"], [\"I6\", \"Buildings with identifiers\"], [\"I7\", \"Vibrancy and dynamics of the ambiance\"], [\"I8\", \"Open views into the wider space\"]], \"views\": [[\"N1\", \"Novo Brdo\"], [\"N2\", \"Litostrojski bloki\"], [\"N3\", \"Mostec\"], [\"N4\", \"Štepanjsko naselje\"], [\"N5\", \"Zupančičeva jama\"]]}</script>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#eef1f3;--card:#fff;--ink:#1b2126;--muted:#5a636b;--accent:#2f5d7c;--line:#d6dde2;--warn:#b3261e;--sel:#dde9f2}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.5 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:22px 16px 40px}\nh1{font-size:1.5rem;margin:0 0 8px}h2{font-size:1.15rem;margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--muted)}\n.card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:18px;margin-top:14px}\n.btn{appearance:none;border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 20px;font:inherit;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;background:var(--accent);color:#fff}\n.btn:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:not-allowed}\n.prog{font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px}\n.win{border:10px solid #e9e4da;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px #cfc8bb;background:#e9e4da}\n.win img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}\n.def{background:var(--sel);border-radius:10px;padding:10px 12px;color:var(--ink);font-size:.95rem}\nlabel.opt{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:9px 12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;margin-top:6px;cursor:pointer}\nlabel.opt:has(input:checked){background:var(--sel);border-color:var(--accent)}\n.blk.miss{outline:2px solid var(--warn);outline-offset:4px;border-radius:8px}\n.err{color:var(--warn);margin-top:8px;min-height:1.2em}\n.credit{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 16px 24px;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted)}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main id=\"app\" aria-live=\"polite\"><p>Loading…</p></main>\n<footer class=\"credit\">Photographs and indicators: Fikfak, Zbašnik-Senegačnik &amp; Drobne (2022), Land 11(12): 2157, Figure 2 and Section 2.3 (doi:10.3390/land11122157, CC BY 4.0).</footer>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var KEY='window-imageability:state', VIEWS=['N1','N2','N3','N4','N5'];\n  var DEF='Imageability means the characteristic and qualitative elements that, when seen in a specific location, attract attention, evoke pleasant feelings and create a memorable impression.';\n  var app=document.getElementById('app'), Q={}, files={}, st=null;\n  function esc(s){return String(s==null?'':s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g,function(c){return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;'}[c];});}\n  function err(m){var e=app.querySelector('.err');if(e)e.textContent=m||'';}\n  function ok(r){return !(r&&r.ok===false);}\n  function save(){try{localStorage.setItem(KEY,JSON.stringify(st));}catch(e){}}\n  function send(list,b,next){if(b)b.disabled=true;Promise.all(list).then(function(rs){var bad=rs.filter(function(r){return !ok(r);})[0];if(bad){if(b)b.disabled=false;return err(bad.error);}next();});}\n  function fresh(){return {step:'intro',group:Math.random()<0.5?'SA1':'SA2',k:0};}\n  function intro(){\n    var multi=st.group==='SA2';\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Window views</h1><p>Imagine you are at home, looking out of your window at the building opposite. You will see five such window views from residential neighbourhoods. For each view, say which '+(multi?'elements make':'element makes')+' the view imageable.</p><p class=\"def\">'+esc(DEF)+'</p><p>'+(multi?'You may choose as many elements as you like for each view.':'Choose one element for each view.')+' It takes about 3 minutes.</p>'+\n     '<div class=\"card\"><label class=\"opt\" style=\"margin-top:0\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"ok\"> '+esc(Q.consent.title)+'</label><div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Start</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){if(!document.getElementById('ok').checked)return err('Consent is needed to continue.');\n      send([SPSite.answer('consent',true),SPSite.answer('group',st.group)],this,function(){st.step='view';st.k=0;save();route();});};\n  }\n  function view(){\n    if(st.k>=VIEWS.length){st.step='about';save();return route();}\n    var id=VIEWS[st.k],f=files[id],multi=st.group==='SA2',q=multi?Q.imageability_multi:Q.imageability_single;\n    app.innerHTML='<div class=\"prog\">Window view '+(st.k+1)+' of '+VIEWS.length+'</div><div class=\"win\"><img alt=\"Window view\" src=\"'+esc(f.url)+'\"></div>'+\n     '<div class=\"card\"><h2>'+esc(q.title)+'</h2><p style=\"margin:0;font-size:.9rem\">'+esc(DEF)+'</p><div class=\"blk\" data-n=\"ind\">'+(q.choices||[]).map(function(c){return '<label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"'+(multi?'checkbox':'radio')+'\" name=\"ind\" value=\"'+esc(c.value)+'\"> '+esc(c.text)+'</label>';}).join('')+'</div>'+\n     '<div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">'+(st.k<VIEWS.length-1?'Next view':'Continue')+'</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){\n      var xs=[].slice.call(app.querySelectorAll('input[name=ind]:checked')).map(function(x){return x.value;});\n      if(!xs.length){app.querySelector('.blk').classList.add('miss');return err(multi?'Please choose at least one element.':'Please choose one element.');}\n      var a=multi?SPSite.answer('imageability_multi',xs,{key:id,shown:[f.name]}):SPSite.answer('imageability_single',xs[0],{key:id,shown:[f.name]});\n      send([a],this,function(){st.k++;save();route();});};\n  }\n  function about(){\n    var q=Q.field;\n    app.innerHTML='<h2>About you</h2><div class=\"card\"><div class=\"blk\" data-n=\"field\"><b>'+esc(q.title)+'</b>'+(q.choices||[]).map(function(c){return '<label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"field\" value=\"'+esc(c.value)+'\"> '+esc(c.text)+'</label>';}).join('')+'</div><div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Finish</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){var x=app.querySelector('input[name=field]:checked');if(!x){app.querySelector('.blk').classList.add('miss');return err('Please choose one.');}\n      send([SPSite.answer('field',x.value)],this,function(){st.step='done';save();route();});};\n  }\n  function finish(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Thank you!</h1><div class=\"card\"><p id=\"fin\">Submitting…</p><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    SPSite.complete().then(function(r){if(!ok(r)){err(r.error||'Some answers are missing.');setTimeout(function(){st.step='intro';save();route();},1800);}\n      else{try{localStorage.removeItem(KEY);}catch(e){}var s=document.getElementById('fin');if(s)s.textContent='Your answers are saved.';}});\n  }\n  app.addEventListener('change',function(e){var r=e.target.closest&&e.target.closest('.blk');if(r){r.classList.remove('miss');err('');}});\n  function route(){var s=st.step;window.scrollTo(0,0);if(s==='view')return view();if(s==='about')return about();if(s==='done')return finish();intro();}\n  SPSite.onReady(function(ctx){\n    ['consent','group','imageability_single','imageability_multi','field'].forEach(function(n){Q[n]=SPSite.getQuestion(n)||{};});\n    (SPSite.getMedia('views')||[]).forEach(function(f){files[f.name.replace(/\\.[^.]+$/,'')]=f;});\n    var need=VIEWS.filter(function(k){return !files[k];});\n    if(need.length){app.innerHTML='<h1>Images missing</h1><p>Upload '+esc(need.join(', '))+' (.jpg) to the media folder \"views\".</p>';return;}\n    try{st=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY));}catch(e){st=null;}\n    var a=(ctx&&ctx.answers)||{};\n    if(!(st&&st.group)||a.consent!==true)st=fresh();\n    save();route();\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
